      {
        "position": 5,
        "title": "works well for my doodle",
        "text": "Works but it feels a little aggressive. Honestly, I wouldn't use it on regular combing, but if you're trying to get matted hair out, this works really well. The blades are fairly sharp and they cut the hair out without too many issues. My pet doesn't seem to think it's too uncomfortable. The blade quality seems pretty solid. I haven't used the hand brush yet, but the fine tooth comb brush is pretty helpful in detangling and also deshedding my dog.",
        "rating": 4,
        "date": "August 6, 2026",
        "author": "Nick Nolte",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHAJPOVAZEE7LT5QIYS7QV2T36KA?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
